          analogy: 'DFA vending machine jaisa hai: 5 Rs ka coin daala toh state change hui, 10 Rs par packet nikal aaya (Accept state)! Har input par exactly EK specific state transition hota hai!',
          simpleExplanation: '• DFA (Deterministic Finite Automata): 5-tuple (Q, Sigma, delta, q0, F). delta: Q x Sigma -> Q (Deterministic: exactly 1 transition for each symbol).\n• NFA (Non-Deterministic): delta: Q x Sigma -> 2^Q (Can transition to 0, 1, or multiple states simultaneously).\n• NFA to DFA (Subset Construction): DFA states are power sets of NFA states. Start with {q0}; for each DFA state and input symbol, find reachable set of NFA states; mark any state containing an NFA final state as a DFA final state.\n• Minimization of DFA: Table-filling (Myhill-Nerode) algorithm merges indistinguishable states.',
          keyFormulasOrKeywords: ['DFA: δ: Q × Σ → Q', 'NFA: δ: Q × Σ → 2^Q', 'Subset Construction creates 2^n states', 'Minimization merges equivalent states'],
