          simpleExplanation: '• Regular Expression: Operators: Union (+), Concatenation (.), Kleene Star (*). Arden\'s Theorem: R = Q + R*P has unique solution R = Q*P*.\n• Pumping Lemma for Regular Languages:\n  - If L is regular, there exists pumping length p such that any string w in L with |w| >= p can be split into w = xyz satisfying:\n    1. |y| > 0 (y is non-empty),\n    2. |xy| <= p,\n    3. x y^i z is in L for all i >= 0.\n  - Used to prove a language is NOT regular by finding a contradiction!',
