          simpleExplanation: '• CFG: G = (V, T, P, S). Productions A -> alpha.\n• Ambiguity: If a string has more than one leftmost derivation or parse tree.\n• Simplification of CFG: (1) Remove useless symbols, (2) Remove null productions (A -> epsilon), (3) Remove unit productions (A -> B).\n• Chomsky Normal Form (CNF): Every production is of the form A -> BC or A -> a.\n• Greibach Normal Form (GNF): Every production starts with a terminal: A -> a alpha.',
          keyFormulasOrKeywords: ['CNF form: A -> BC or A -> a', 'GNF form: A -> a α', 'Remove null (ε) -> unit -> useless symbols'],
