          simpleExplanation: '• PDA = Finite Automaton + 1 Infinite Stack memory: 7-tuple (Q, Sigma, Gamma, delta, q0, z0, F).\n• Transition delta(q, a, X) = (p, alpha): State changes to p, top stack symbol X is replaced by string alpha.\n• Acceptance: By Final State OR by Empty Stack (both are equivalent in computational power).\n• Deterministic PDA (DPDA) vs Non-Deterministic PDA (NPDA): NPDA is strictly more powerful than DPDA (e.g. even-length palindromes WW^R require NPDA).',
          keyFormulasOrKeywords: ['PDA = DFA + Stack', 'Delta: Q × (Σ ∪ {ε}) × Γ → 2^(Q × Γ*)', 'Acceptance: Final State vs Empty Stack', 'NPDA > DPDA power'],
