          simpleExplanation: '• Turing Machine (7-tuple): Infinite tape divided into cells + Read/Write head that can move Left (L) or Right (R).\n• delta(q, X) = (p, Y, D): In state q, reading symbol X, write symbol Y, transition to state p, and move head in direction D (L or R).\n• Halting: TM halts when it reaches an accept state (Halts & Accepts) or no transition defined (Halts & Rejects).\n• Halting Problem of Turing Machine: Proven Undecidable by Alan Turing using Diagonalization (no algorithm can determine whether an arbitrary program will halt or loop forever).',
